## Plan Overview

8-phase incremental backend rework aligned with multi-layer caching architecture.
Phases 1-3 are highest priority. Phases 4-8 follow in order.
Each phase is independently shippable and backward-compatible.

---

## Phase 1: Cache Platform Foundation ⬅️ START HERE
**Goal:** Create unified `CacheService` abstraction, fix existing bugs, eliminate duplication.

### 1.1 Create CacheService abstraction (`lib/cache/cache-service.ts`)
- [ ] Define `CachePolicy` interface: `{ ttl, staleTtl, layer, invalidationMode, version }`
- [ ] Define `CacheLayer` enum: `'memory' | 'redis' | 'cdn'`
- [ ] Define `InvalidationMode` enum: `'write-aside' | 'write-through' | 'ttl-only'`
- [ ] Implement `CacheService` class with methods:
  - `getOrLoad<T>(key, loader, policy)` — read-through with singleflight
  - `set<T>(key, value, policy)` — write to appropriate layers
  - `invalidate(key)` — delete from all layers
  - `invalidateNamespace(namespace)` — versioned namespace flush
  - `get<T>(key)` — raw get (no loader)
- [ ] Versioned key format: `qunt:v2:{domain}:{scope}:{id}`
- [ ] In-memory layer: LRU Map with configurable max entries (default 500)
- [ ] Redis layer: reuse existing 3-tier fallback (memory → local Redis → Upstash)
- [ ] Singleflight: in-process dedup per key (Map<key, Promise>)
- [ ] Stale-while-recompute: serve stale up to `staleTtl` past TTL while one refresher runs

### 1.2 Fix existing cache bugs
- [ ] Fix AI cache namespace=key bug in `lib/ai/cache.ts` (passes `cacheKey` as both namespace AND key)
- [ ] Fix duplicate `queryCache` Map in `redis-client.ts` and `query-optimizer.ts`
- [ ] Add missing `cacheLife` to `server/tags.ts` `_getTagsCached`
- [ ] Add missing `cacheTag` to `server/dashboard-bootstrap.ts` `getDashboardBootstrap`
- [ ] Fix inconsistent dashboard layout TTLs (`user-data.ts` uses 120/120/600, `layouts.ts` uses 300/300/1800)
- [ ] Fix `ACCOUNT_METRICS` tag defined but never used on read
- [ ] Fix `prop-firms-catalogue` tag never invalidated by admin CRUD

### 1.3 Graceful degradation
- [ ] On Redis failure: log once per window with request/key/layer context, skip cache writes, fall back to DB
- [ ] Invalidation remains idempotent and best-effort: DB commit first, then updateTag + Redis delete; cache failure never rolls back write
- [ ] Add circuit breaker for Redis (track failures, skip Redis for 30s after N consecutive failures)

### 1.4 Migrate existing callers to CacheService
- [ ] Migrate `lib/ai/cache.ts` to use CacheService
- [ ] Migrate `lib/query-optimizer.ts` to use CacheService (or delete if truly unused)
- [ ] Migrate Redis namespace invalidation calls in `server/trades.ts` to CacheService
- [ ] Keep `'use cache'`/`updateTag` for SSR reads (do NOT replace)
- [ ] Clean up dead code: `executeOptimizedQuery` if unused

### Verification
- [ ] `npx tsc --noEmit` passes
- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
- [ ] `bun run build` passes
- [ ] Unit tests for CacheService: getOrLoad, set, invalidate, singleflight, stale serving, Redis failure fallback
- [ ] Existing functionality preserved (deals page, dashboard, AI chat all work)

---

## Phase 2: Cache Policy Standardization & Hot-Surface Migration
**Goal:** Define cache policies by data class and migrate highest-value surfaces.

### 2.1 Define cache policies
- [ ] Public reference data (deals, firms, propfirm stats): CDN `s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=600`, Redis TTL 300s, memory TTL 30s, write-aside invalidation
- [ ] Private summaries (behavior insights, dashboard trade summaries, user-data snapshots): Redis TTL 60s, memory TTL 15s, no CDN, write-aside invalidation
- [ ] AI-derived data (trade-context helpers): Redis TTL 90s, namespace invalidation on trade writes
- [ ] Critical entitlement (subscription summary): Redis TTL 30s, write-through on webhook/admin plan changes, no stale serving

### 2.2 Migrate route families (incremental)
- [ ] Public deals APIs and prop-firm read models
- [ ] Private analytics reads (behavior/insights, dashboard trade summaries)
- [ ] AI trade-history/context loaders
- [ ] Remaining read-heavy admin/report endpoints

### 2.3 Measure and validate
- [ ] Measure baseline latency for each route family before migration
- [ ] Measure hit rate and latency after migration
- [ ] Target: 3x improvement on warm hits, >=80% steady-state hit rate on migrated routes
- [ ] Retire unused/duplicate cache helpers as each family is absorbed

### Verification
- [ ] All Phase 1 checks pass
- [ ] Cache hit/miss metrics visible in logs
- [ ] No correctness regressions (stale data within TTL bounds)

---

## Phase 3: API Hardening with `withApiRoute`
**Goal:** Normalize API route handling, error responses, request tracking.

### 3.1 Create `withApiRoute` wrapper (`lib/api/with-api-route.ts`)
- [ ] Request ID creation (`X-Request-Id` header)
- [ ] Structured logging with request context (route, method, userId, requestId)
- [ ] Latency measurement and logging (`http_request_duration_ms`)
- [ ] Auth integration (Supabase session extraction)
- [ ] Rate limiting integration
- [ ] Zod schema validation helper
- [ ] `apiError`/`apiSuccess` envelope standardization
- [ ] `Cache-Status` response header
- [ ] Body size limit enforcement

### 3.2 Standardize error response format
- [ ] All routes use `{ error: { code, message, requestId } }` format
- [ ] Fix 3 inconsistent patterns: `apiError()`, direct JSON, raw `new Response()`
- [ ] Fix IBKR routes using raw `new Response(JSON.stringify(...))`

### 3.3 Apply wrapper to highest-value routes
- [ ] Checkout/payment routes (`/api/whop/checkout`, `/api/whop/checkout-team`)
- [ ] Invitation/team routes (`/api/team/invite`, `/api/team/accept-invitation`)
- [ ] Deals routes (all 4)
- [ ] Dashboard data routes (`/api/dashboard/trades`, `/api/dashboard/accounts`)
- [ ] Admin/report routes

### 3.4 Add pagination defaults
- [ ] Default page size: 50, max page size: 200 on all list endpoints
- [ ] Enforce `take`/`skip` on all unbounded `findMany` calls

### Verification
- [ ] All wrapped routes return `X-Request-Id` header
- [ ] All wrapped routes return consistent error format
- [ ] Latency metrics logged for every wrapped route
- [ ] Backward compatible (existing response bodies unchanged)

---

## Phase 4: Mutation Safety & Idempotency
**Goal:** Add idempotency support for externally-retried mutation endpoints.

### 4.1 Create IdempotencyService (`lib/idempotency.ts`)
- [ ] `Idempotency-Key` header support on POST endpoints
- [ ] Store idempotency records in Postgres (durable, not Redis)
- [ ] Schema: `{ key (unique), endpoint, requestHash, response, createdAt, expiresAt }`
- [ ] Auto-expire records older than 24h via TTL column
- [ ] On duplicate key: return stored response

### 4.2 Apply to target endpoints
- [ ] `POST /api/whop/checkout`
- [ ] `POST /api/whop/checkout-team`
- [ ] `POST /api/team/invite`
- [ ] Other externally-retried mutation endpoints

### 4.3 Unify webhook dedup
- [ ] Move webhook idempotency (`processedWebhook` table) under same service boundary
- [ ] One dedup pattern for both webhook and non-webhook paths

### Verification
- [ ] Duplicate `Idempotency-Key` returns same response
- [ ] Expired keys are treated as new requests
- [ ] Webhook dedup still works correctly

---

## Phase 5: Rate Limiting & Query Bounds
**Goal:** Close rate limiting gaps, enforce bounded queries.

### 5.1 Route-class policy matrix
- [ ] Public read: 120/min per IP
- [ ] Authenticated read: 120/min per user
- [ ] Authenticated write: 30/min per user
- [ ] Admin: 120/min read, 30/min write
- [ ] AI: keep existing per-route limits
- [ ] Webhook/cron: auth-only (no rate limit)

### 5.2 Fix ~30 routes with NO rate limiting
- [ ] `/api/dashboard/trades`, `/api/dashboard/accounts`
- [ ] `/api/deals/*` (all 4 routes)
- [ ] `/api/behavior/insights`, `/api/trader-profile/benchmark`
- [ ] `/api/referral`, `/api/user/theme`
- [ ] `/api/tradovate/synchronizations`, `/api/rithmic/encryption-key`
- [ ] Email routes (IBKR extract-orders, fifo-computation)
- [ ] Team analytics routes

### 5.3 Enforce bounded queries
- [ ] Eliminate unbounded `findMany` on: `_getUnifiedFirms`, `_listPropFirms`, `loadTradesPage` stats, `equity-chart.ts` trades, `calculateAccountMetricsAction`, `getTeamOverviewData`
- [ ] Add `take` limits or pagination to all list endpoints
- [ ] Push filters to DB where currently done in JS (equity-chart date/instrument/tag filters)

### Verification
- [ ] Every API route has rate limiting or explicit exemption
- [ ] No unbounded Prisma queries remain
- [ ] Load test confirms rate limiting works

---

## Phase 6: Data Access Refactoring
**Goal:** Extract repositories, optimize queries, add indexes.

### 6.1 Extract read repositories
- [ ] `server/repositories/deals-repository.ts` — deals/prop-firms read queries
- [ ] `server/repositories/trade-summaries-repository.ts` — trade summary aggregations
- [ ] `server/repositories/subscription-repository.ts` — subscription/entitlement reads
- [ ] `server/repositories/team-analytics-repository.ts` — team analytics queries

### 6.2 Optimize critical queries
- [ ] Push equity-chart filters to DB (currently loads ALL trades, filters in JS)
- [ ] Fix `loadTradesPage` stats query (unbounded PnL fetch → SQL window function for winning streak)
- [ ] Consolidate `getTeamOverviewData` N+1 (team > members > user > accounts > trades)
- [ ] Consolidate `updateTeamAnalytics` 6+ queries into 1-2 aggregate queries
- [ ] Fix `calculateAccountMetricsAction` missing `select` projection
- [ ] Consolidate duplicate user resolution (3 files × 2 queries each → shared resolver)

### 6.3 Add measured indexes
- [ ] Run `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` on highest-latency queries
- [ ] Add `PropFirm.isActive` index
- [ ] Add `PropFirmCoupon.isActive` + `PropFirmCoupon.expiresAt` indexes (if measured benefit)
- [ ] Add `PropFirmReview.status` index (if measured benefit)
- [ ] Only add indexes backed by measured query plans

### Verification
- [ ] Query latency improvements measured (before/after)
- [ ] No N+1 patterns remaining in hot paths
- [ ] `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` confirms index usage

